1
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:07,637
That's...Giorno's brooch?

2
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:09,837
C-could it be...alive?

3
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,120
I can't believe it!

4
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:13,197
It's forming a brand new hand!

5
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:16,117
Giorno's not going down
without a hell of a fight!

6
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,857
As long as I keep that
thing away from his hand,

7
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:20,577
Narancia and Mista might have a chance!

8
00:00:20,660 --> 00:00:22,437
But how the hell do I do that?

9
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:23,937
What am I gonna do?!

10
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:29,100
God bless you.

11
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:21,800
And if you are the best man,

12
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:26,317
You can't break it and move on.

13
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:29,060
Woah, woah...

14
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:32,097
The miracles that make us.

15
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:33,260
To the world,

16
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:35,637
Don't care.

17
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:39,957
The peace of the door,
The body who will die.

18
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,517
The hope that we can live.

19
00:01:42,600 --> 00:01:44,300
Hell no!

20
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:04,560
I must not utter a single sound.

21
00:02:05,020 --> 00:02:07,437
And I can't move any
faster than the brooch,

22
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:10,108
or that thing will zero
in on me and attack.

23
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:14,497
I'm so sorry everyone
but I can't do anything

24
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:17,597
to help once it feeds
on the brooch it'll go

25
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:20,797
after me next now's my
chance to get out of

26
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:26,617
sight the closet I can
hide in there for now this

27
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:31,077
switch it must be the
chair's recline button of

28
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:33,697
course this will be my
ticket out of this nightmare

29
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:37,057
situation that beast
will catch sight of the

30
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,846
seat moving and shift
its focus to go after it

31
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:43,557
then i'll grab the brooch
and rush to the cockpit

32
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:47,637
what am i thinking i
can't do something like

33
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:50,717
that it's madness talk
about having a death

34
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:54,740
wish forget it i'll wait
this out in the closet

35
00:02:56,780 --> 00:02:59,956
have i lost it it's like my
body just acted on its own

36
00:03:05,020 --> 00:03:06,432
This isn't making sense.

37
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,424
I was determined to not press the
button, but then did it anyway.

38
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:11,750
Fine.

39
00:03:11,833 --> 00:03:12,680
I'm gonna go for it.

40
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,180
It's now or never.

41
00:03:15,380 --> 00:03:16,380
All right, Trish.

42
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:17,420
Take your time.

43
00:03:18,480 --> 00:03:21,720
Move nice and slow, like a Tai Chi master.

44
00:03:23,580 --> 00:03:24,410
Almost there.

45
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,075
Just two more meters.

46
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,276
Slow and deliberate.

47
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:29,992
Your life depends on it.

48
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:33,737
It's coming this way.

49
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:35,877
Shit, it already destroyed the seat!

50
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:37,901
Which means no more reclining it.

51
00:03:39,220 --> 00:03:40,050
Don't panic.

52
00:03:40,133 --> 00:03:41,904
Just make another seat recline.

53
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:51,950
What?

54
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:54,453
Why did it go after me and not the seat?

55
00:03:57,700 --> 00:03:58,818
What's this liquid?

56
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:02,817
Did that fleshy horror react
to it dripping to the ground?

57
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:05,782
But why are my boots even
wet in the first place?

58
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:08,337
All I did was push the recline button.

59
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:10,655
So how the hell did they get drenched?

60
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,630
Damn it!

61
00:04:14,740 --> 00:04:18,622
This is exactly why I didn't want
to go after that stupid ladybug!

62
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:21,902
I should have just stayed
out of this altogether!

63
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:25,960
Help me to drag me!

64
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,120
I'm going to die!

65
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:43,857
What my boot just fell
off my foot it's like

66
00:04:43,940 --> 00:04:46,897
it slid around and passed through my leg I

67
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:50,337
don't understand any of
this what just happened

68
00:04:50,420 --> 00:04:55,720
here's your opportunity procure
the brooch Quickly, Trish.

69
00:04:57,760 --> 00:04:58,600
Who's there?

70
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,791
Who's speaking right now?

71
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:03,480
Someone who's always been here.

72
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:09,380
Since you were a little girl,
never once have I left your side.

73
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:13,540
Now, Trish, I'm asking you
to retrieve that brooch.

74
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:17,429
You've already made
the decision, you know.

75
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:21,400
Protecting Giorno's hand
started you down this road.

76
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,180
But your hesitation weakens you.

77
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,340
Act now.

78
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:27,400
What would you have me do?

79
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,657
Tell me, Trish. I...

80
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:31,505
I don't even know who you are.

81
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,016
That's quite simple.

82
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,340
I am your essence.

83
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:37,817
I am the force who repelled
that scum from your boot.

84
00:05:37,900 --> 00:05:39,640
Your inner power given form.

85
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:42,540
Think of me as your unique ability. Huh?

86
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:45,840
Now, you've made your decision, so act.

87
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:48,260
You must protect Giorno's hand.

88
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,100
Get to it!

89
00:05:51,020 --> 00:05:55,961
But Trish, by keeping it from harm, you
give Giorno and the others a chance at life.

90
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:58,584
And it gives you a chance, too.

91
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,440
What is happening?

92
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,560
Pick it up now! Hurry!

93
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,340
I'm about to die!

94
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:13,798
I don't know what to do or
how to protect this thing!

95
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:19,480
You do know what to do, Trish.

96
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:22,218
Our ability made the seat malleable.

97
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:35,950
What?

98
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:38,510
Malleable?

99
00:06:38,860 --> 00:06:42,520
I know it's crazy, but I just
slipped right through the seat.

100
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,828
And I heard that
abomination in the process.

101
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:49,200
My powers ripped off a chunk of its body.

102
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,440
It can stop bullets,

103
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,237
catch up to a speeding plane,

104
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:57,085
and even annihilate objects moving
at high speeds without issue.

105
00:06:57,260 --> 00:07:01,319
But when it hits a still object, it
breaks apart like hamburger meat.

106
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:03,040
Are you actually me?

107
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:04,660
I mean my essence.

108
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:07,020
And did I really just do all this?

109
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:08,777
My boot slipping off my foot.

110
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:09,977
That doesn't matter.

111
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:10,890
Not right now.

112
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:12,809
You've secured the brooch.

113
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:15,840
Your deep determination
overcame your cowardice.

114
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:18,137
You are growing much stronger, Trish.

115
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:20,360
Mentally and emotionally as well.

116
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:21,938
It's lovely to see.

117
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,430
Listen.

118
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:28,180
Your power is to transform any
matter into a malleable object.

119
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:30,620
The power to make things soft.

120
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:33,940
Yet even more durable than diamonds.

121
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:38,600
Here it comes!

122
00:07:38,860 --> 00:07:40,801
You must remain completely still.

123
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:43,512
I finally get that we're the same entity.

124
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,737
But I've got to get out of sight!

125
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:49,300
Please, make the closet elastic! Hurry!

126
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,461
I'm begging you!

127
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:51,940
Stay away!

128
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,460
You're not getting in here! Get back!

129
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:08,340
Shit, it managed to sniff me out all
the way back here. I'm... I'm dead.

130
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:11,949
I know I'm supposed to
be a stand user now,

131
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:14,457
and I can use all of these
special powers or whatever.

132
00:08:14,540 --> 00:08:16,857
But what good are they?

133
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:18,617
This thing's unstoppable!

134
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:21,077
Its users already dead!

135
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:21,990
For heaven's sakes!

136
00:08:22,073 --> 00:08:24,600
Nothing can stop this murderous blob!

137
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:31,517
You see, this is why I
asked you to remain still.

138
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:34,877
Earlier, our primary
duty should be reaching!

139
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:38,277
But we went the other direction!

140
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:40,077
What are you talking about?

141
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:41,717
Journo's brooch is nothing but!

142
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,717
of Robbing Incubator at the moment.

143
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,160
I had to rescue it.

144
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:47,598
All this power does is soften stuff.

145
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:49,055
It's totally useless!

146
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:51,321
I can barely dodge these attacks!

147
00:08:57,060 --> 00:08:57,890
Huh?

148
00:08:58,580 --> 00:09:00,345
It went after the clock again?

149
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:02,170
What the?

150
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,897
The clock has been elasticized huh?

151
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:15,437
As long as your movements don't
exceed the speed of the second hand,

152
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,817
the clock should hold the
attention of the enemy,

153
00:09:17,900 --> 00:09:20,957
giving you an opportunity to
escape and rush to the cockpit.

154
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:25,537
I told you to remain
still, but I misspoke.

155
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:27,760
I meant to move stealthily.

156
00:09:28,980 --> 00:09:31,215
Slower than the second hand, at least.

157
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:35,600
In truth, you must move as
slowly as a glacier in winter.

158
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:40,000
All the while possessing
the power of an iron vice.

159
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:44,177
Time to pulverize this
rotten heap of meat.

160
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:46,380
I want to hear it scream.

161
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,257
Paris di merda.

162
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:53,040
Why don't you do us all
a favor and just die?

163
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:58,240
Make this easy on yourself We both
know you want to croak, so do it!

164
00:09:58,380 --> 00:09:59,400
Die already!

165
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:04,920
It's breaking down into tiny pieces.

166
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:06,500
Is it evaporating?

167
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:08,713
After all that trouble,

168
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:13,260
this vile killer of a stand is now
just a pile of disintegrating flesh.

169
00:10:19,600 --> 00:10:21,700
Um, what's your name?

170
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:24,600
I mean, do you have one?

171
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:27,560
If we're a team, what do I call you?

172
00:10:28,760 --> 00:10:30,300
Call me Spicy Lady.

173
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:33,170
Huh.

174
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:35,651
Weird, but in a good way.

175
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:08,472
Thanks to your bravery, Mista and
Narancia won't die from their wounds now.

176
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,400
You know, Giorno Giovanna
sure is a special one.

177
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:15,460
Without a doubt, he's a giver of life.

178
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:18,020
But in addition, he is a catalyst.

179
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:20,695
Watching him has caused you to mature.

180
00:11:34,740 --> 00:11:37,564
I'll make sure the engines
are working properly.

181
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:42,057
Luchirati, there's something
that you ought to know.

182
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:44,022
There's no need for us to worry.

183
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:46,177
Giorno's already begun his plan to...

184
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:48,319
Triss, whatever it is, it can wait!

185
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:50,510
Listen up.

186
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,060
Move slowly.

187
00:11:52,780 --> 00:11:55,660
It's crucial that you
carefully inch toward me.

188
00:11:55,860 --> 00:11:57,280
We're at 7,000 meters.

189
00:11:58,520 --> 00:11:59,400
6,800.

190
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,040
6,600.

191
00:12:02,040 --> 00:12:02,870
Damn it.

192
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:06,532
We're dropping like a sack of
rocks, but I don't know why.

193
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:09,640
As to why we're losing
altitude, I have the answer.

194
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:14,580
But even so, I'm at a complete
loss regarding what to do about it.

195
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:17,640
I hate to say it, but I'm stumped here.

196
00:12:18,060 --> 00:12:20,337
What the heck are you
talking about, Bucurati?

197
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:22,067
What did I say about moving?

198
00:12:22,600 --> 00:12:23,430
No.

199
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:24,580
Please, no.

200
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:27,040
Wait, what? There's no way.

201
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:29,177
How the hell did it even...

202
00:12:29,260 --> 00:12:32,220
Giorno said the beast
latches onto moving objects.

203
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,557
Once they're captured, it devours them.

204
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:36,097
Right now, the plane's engines...

205
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:38,380
In a word, they've been... eaten!

206
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:46,600
Trish, keep looking forward.

207
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,520
You must remain calm.

208
00:12:49,160 --> 00:12:52,120
Just keep moving toward me, nice and slow.

209
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:02,390
What's this?

210
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:05,320
What the hell is this monster?

211
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:07,337
It can't stop us from falling.

212
00:13:07,420 --> 00:13:10,773
We're about to get up close
and personal with the ground.

213
00:13:10,860 --> 00:13:13,037
Actually, we'd be lucky to hit the ground.

214
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:14,497
These engines are going to blow.

215
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:15,698
How did it survive?

216
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:18,160
It was torn to pieces and evaporated.

217
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:20,460
Shit, that's right.

218
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:23,093
The engine is located behind the closet.

219
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:24,970
Oh no.

220
00:13:25,053 --> 00:13:29,017
A cell or two must have passed through
a crevice in the wall of the closet.

221
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:32,924
It must be having a field day
feeding on the power of the engine.

222
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:34,137
And now...

223
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:36,140
We're gonna have to crash land.

224
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,200
Aim for the Terranian Sea.

225
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,207
Prepare for a water landing.

226
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:41,498
It's our only hope.

227
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,940
An emergency landing.

228
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:48,907
Even if by some miracle we manage to land
on the water in one piece, then what?

229
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,962
It'll still try to hunt us down.

230
00:13:51,320 --> 00:13:53,840
I can't find any weaknesses in this stand.

231
00:13:54,140 --> 00:13:55,140
It's unstoppable.

232
00:13:56,440 --> 00:13:57,920
Slow and steady, Trish.

233
00:13:58,520 --> 00:13:59,360
Easy does it.

234
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:02,472
Move like a tiger closing in on its prey.

235
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:04,040
Calm and deliberate.

236
00:14:05,020 --> 00:14:05,850
Don't run.

237
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,456
Doing so will just invite its attack.

238
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:14,420
What are you doing?

239
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:15,597
Weren't you listening?

240
00:14:15,680 --> 00:14:17,077
It's gonna latch onto you!

241
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,217
Yeah, you're damn right it
will, but what does it matter?

242
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:22,777
The same thing will happen
even if I move like a slug.

243
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,448
So why not take the gamble?

244
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:27,642
Now get your ass back in
the cockpit, Butcherati!

245
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,941
You've completely lost your mind!

246
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:31,160
The door's not...

247
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,280
How the hell?

248
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:38,640
Miss Power. Don't tell me.

249
00:14:38,960 --> 00:14:40,477
This girl is...

250
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,980
An emergency landing?

251
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:44,837
Sorry, but you've got the wrong idea.

252
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:48,697
If you want to live long enough to
see Sardinia with your own eyes,

253
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:50,337
we've no choice but to...

254
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:51,940
Bust this death trap!

255
00:14:52,880 --> 00:14:53,710
Wannabe!

256
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:56,400
Spicy lady!

257
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:03,580
What in the world? These powers.

258
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,881
When did you get stand abilities?

259
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:10,545
The walls, the glass, everything
in here is elastic like rubber.

260
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:14,517
It's pretty obvious by now that this
meatloaf from Hell has a need for speed.

261
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,740
Well, the bastard's in luck.

262
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:23,620
A plane falling from the sky
